{"id":"1297979843489955845","date":"2020-08-24","url":"https://x.com/leopoldasch/status/1297979843489955845","author":"leopoldasch","text":"@joshgans @trvrb has a good thread on this https://t.co/Mu2OQXukHx","reply_to":"leopoldasch","quoted":{"url":"https://x.com/trvrb/status/1291860659118804992","text":"I wanted to discuss the degree to which population immunity may be contributing to curbing #COVID19 in Florida, Arizona and Texas, where recent surges have resulted in substantial epidemics. 1/16"},"live_status":200,"archived_at":"20200824193223","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200824193223/https://twitter.com/leopoldasch/status/1297979843489955845","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1297979441088528391","date":"2020-08-24","url":"https://x.com/leopoldasch/status/1297979441088528391","author":"leopoldasch","text":"@joshgans The herd immunity threshold can be lower with social distancing. If social distancing drives R0_t from 3 to 1.1, then that leads to an outbreak in places where no one is immune. But if 10% is immune already bc of first wve, then R ends up below 1, and there is no second wave.","reply_to":"joshgans","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20200824193108","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200824193108/https://twitter.com/leopoldasch/status/1297979441088528391","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
